OCGRAPH 1
# THE GAME MODE, as a graph -- identical shape to test-content/AN_Playable's own Rules.ocgraph, kept
# deliberately unchanged: a round clock in a VAR is already a complete demonstration of "a game mode
# as a graph, so the play session starts" and there is nothing FirstPerson-specific to add to it. See
# Rules.ocgraph's own comments for the class-flags history (why `CLASS ... GameMode` genuinely begins
# play today, and did not always) and for what a graph GameMode still cannot do (name a default
# pawn/controller -- this template's player is PLACED, same as AN_Playable's).
#
# ONE THING WORTH KNOWING BEFORE YOU READ A HEADLESS LOG OF THIS PROJECT: you will see TWO 'FPRules'
# entities ticking, not one, even though Content/Maps/Default.ocmap places exactly one. That is not
# this graph misbehaving -- `aver_fw_begin_play` (modules/framework/src/FrameworkAbi.cpp) spawns a
# FRESH instance of whatever class carries the GameMode flag the moment play begins, unconditionally,
# with no awareness that the level's own PLACE line already put one down. Both instances tick off the
# same per-frame deltaTime, so their `elapsed` values track each other exactly -- confirmed against a
# real headless run of AN_Playable, which places `class AN_Rules` the same way and shows the identical
# doubling. Harmless (neither instance's state leaks into the other's), but worth naming rather than
# leaving you to wonder if you miscounted your own placements.
# NAME is a single token (see AN_FPCharacter.ocgraph's own comment on this record).
NAME FPRules
DESCRIPTION The game mode, as a graph. Starts the play session and keeps a round clock in a VAR.

CLASS AN_FPRules GameMode

PARAM deltaTime float

VAR elapsed float 0

NODE dt Param param=deltaTime

ENTRY tick OnTick
NODE tick OnTick

NODE prev GetVar var=elapsed
NODE sum Add
LINK prev.value sum.a
LINK dt.value sum.b

NODE store SetVar var=elapsed
LINK tick.exec store.exec
LINK sum.result store.value

# Read back through its own node after the write, for the reason Target.ocgraph's (and this
# template's own AN_FPTarget.ocgraph's) comments give.
NODE report GetVar var=elapsed
OUT report value
